              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for good fortune, then the Hindi for chance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चौकन्ना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चौकन्ना — caukannā — \"alert, watchful\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जंगल में हिरन हमेशा चौकन्ना रहता है। Jaṅgal meṁ hiran hameśā caukannā rahtā hai. In the forest a deer is always on the alert."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चौकन्ना (caukannā) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit catuṣkarṇa, \"heard by four ears\" (CDIAL 4630). CDIAL gives the Hindi word as \"vigilant, circumspect\": all ears."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
